course: dictionary
lesson: 13297
title: Gratis: free of charge
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you about money. Gratis is one of them. It means free of charge, so you do not have to pay anything. Shops and adverts use it. «You get the second one gratis» tells you that the second one costs nothing.
explain: Look at the words around gratis to check. In «The museum is open gratis on Sundays», the words open and Sundays do not tell you the price, but gratis does. Ask yourself: if I put free of charge in the sentence instead, does it still make sense? If it does, you have found the meaning.
explain: Gratis can be used in more than one way. You can say «You can enter gratis» (it tells how you enter) or «The tickets were gratis» (it tells what the tickets are like). You will also hear the phrases for gratis and gratis and for nothing. They mean the same thing.
fact: Gratis means free of charge, without having to pay.
fact: «You get the second one gratis» means you do not pay for the second one.
fact: Gratis can be an adverb («You can enter gratis») or an adjective («The tickets were gratis»).
fact: Phrases with the same meaning: for gratis, gratis and for nothing.
fact: Gratis is used in shops, adverts and sometimes as a jokey word in speech, which is why you will meet it often.
exercise: «The museum is open gratis on Sundays.» What does gratis mean? | Closed for the winter | Very late | Open all day and night | *Free of charge
exercise: The leaflet said, «Entry is gratis for children.» What does gratis tell you? | *Children do not have to pay | Children get a prize | Children must wait outside | Children must bring money
exercise: Which phrase has the same meaning as gratis? | Twice over | Half price | Costing a lot | *For nothing
test: Mum says, «The second cake is gratis.» What must she mean? | It is the biggest cake | You must pay double for it | *You do not have to pay for it | It is stale and old
test: «Gratis parking all day!» says the sign. What does the sign tell drivers? | Parking costs extra | *Parking is free, so you pay nothing | The car park is full | Parking is only at night
exam: The advert says, «Gratis parking all day!» What does gratis mean here? | Parking costs extra | Parking is underground | Parking is full | *Free, so you pay nothing to park
